<title>USA: US Treasury 5-yr note seen yielding 6.32/6.33 pct.</title>
<headline>US Treasury 5-yr note seen yielding 6.32/6.33 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's auction of $12.5 billion in five-year notes on Thursday is expected to produce a yield between 6.32 and 6.33 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>The offering will settle January 31 and raise $3.2 billion in new money.</p>
<p>At 1234 EST/1734 GMT, the five-year notes were quoted at 6.33 percent in when-issued trade.</p>
<p>The bidding deadline for the notes is 1300 EST/1800 GMT and results are expected around 1345 EST/1845 GMT.</p>
<p>(( N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
